SteamARM: macOS 15's window tiling for X windows

X windows are drawn by quartz-wm through Xplugin; they are not NSWindows,
so macOS's own tiling never applied to them. Here it is in the window
manager, for framed windows and for frameless ones that move through
_NET_WM_MOVERESIZE (Steam's, Chromium's, SDL's):

- drag a window's title bar to an edge of the screen: left or right edge,
  that half; top edge, Fill; near a corner, that quarter. While the pointer
  is there an outline of the region shows (a shaped ring at the floating
  level that takes no input: XQuartz has no translucent windows); release
  tiles the window. QUARTZ_WM_TILING=0 turns the drag tiling off;
- a tiled window dragged away goes back to its size from before, the point
  under the pointer kept in proportion; a resize by hand leaves the tile;
- the regions are the visible frame of the screen (below the menu bar,
  beside the Dock), with the gaps of "Tiled windows have margins"
  (com.apple.WindowManager EnableTiledWindowMargins);
- a double click on the title bar with the macOS setting "Fill" fills the
  window, and a second one gives back its size (Maximize stays Zoom);
- XQuartz's Window menu (patches/xquartz-ui-tiling-menu.patch) sends Fill,
  Center, the halves, the quarters and Return to Previous Size as an
  AppleWMControllerNotify of kind 32 (QWM_TILE_KIND), the action in arg;
- a drag is decided by where the press was, not by where the pointer is
  once past the threshold: a quick drag was over the client already and
  never moved the window.

Measured with XTest drags: left edge 943x1050 (the visible frame is 1887
wide beside a Dock on the right), top edge Fill 1887x1050, bottom right
corner 943x525, dragged away back to 800x522; a frameless window through
_NET_WM_MOVERESIZE: right half, then back to 700x450.
